{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue moved from $41.9 billion in FY2016 to $47.9 billion in FY2025, a 1.5% CAGR [F1][F10][F219]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step down then a rebuild: revenue fell 13.5% in FY2017 and 5.3% in FY2018, then compounded 3.7% a year from FY2022 to FY2025 [D42][D93][D782]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2017 decline came with refranchising of bottling operations, which cut operating cash flow by 20% that year [P75]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 was the sharpest inflection, with operating income up 37.7% on lower other operating charges after the prior-year fairlife contingent consideration remeasurement [D450][P12]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 concentrate operations contributed 1.6pp of the 1.9% revenue growth and were 59.4% of revenue [D534][D449][D532]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Finished product operations in the US added 1.3pp while non-US finished product operations subtracted 1.0pp [D562][D555]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Worldwide concentrate sales volume grew 1% in FY2025 while unit case volume was even [P16]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 9.7pp slower than revenue in FY2025, at cost of revenue growth of 0.4% and SG&A down 0.4% [D474][D465][D466]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 23.6% against net income growth of 23.3% as the diluted share count fell 0.2% [D453][D451][D468]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 28.7% in FY2025 was above the 26.0% window median and at the window high, versus a 20.7% low in FY2016 [F50][D766][D765][D764]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin of 61.6% sat above its 60.7% window median and below the 62.1% high [F30][D772][D771]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The 7.5pp operating margin gain in FY2025 came mostly from the 6.2pp other-lines residual, reflecting lower other operating charges after the fairlife remeasurement [D463][D477][P12]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 27.3% sat 1.4pp below the 28.7% operating margin, with a 17.9% effective tax rate [F70][F50][D810][D435]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $7.41 billion was 0.57x net income in FY2025, below the 1.18x window median and the window low [F100][D436][D800][D799]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $5.30 billion was a 11.0% margin, below the 20.2% window median [F120][D433][D775]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 collapse to $6.81 billion operating cash flow was driven primarily by the $6.0 billion IRS Tax Litigation Deposit [F99][P22]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $2.11 billion was 4.4% of revenue and 2.01x D&A, the highest multiple in the window [F110][D432][D438]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt was $32.4 billion in FY2023, net cash of -70.7% of revenue, but total debt is not reported after FY2023 so later net cash is omitted [D341][D342][X194]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio rose to 1.46x in FY2025, above the 1.13x window median and at the window high [F200][D781][D780]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $9.53 billion were 179.9% of free cash flow in FY2025, against 65.4% in FY2021 [D444][D445][D242]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 46.0% was above the 36.5% staples peer median, at the 67th percentile of six peers [D448][D798][D797]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue for FY2017 and FY2018 in the table is a later recast, $36.2 billion and $34.3 billion versus $35.4 billion and $31.9 billion first reported [F2][X2][F3][X3]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Growth and margins spanning those years mix two presentations, so the FY2017 and FY2018 comparisons are not clean [R1]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Buybacks and dividends exceeded free cash flow in FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025, at 105.1%, 214.2% and 179.9% [D344][D395][D445]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Payout above free cash flow for three years leaves little room if conversion stays weak [R2]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Free cash flow ran below 80% of net income in FY2024 and FY2025, at 0.45x and 0.40x [D387][D437]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Cash conversion at the window low is the metric that most undercuts the earnings growth story [R3]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating cash flow to net income recovers above the 1.18x window median from 0.57x in FY2025, in the FY2026 10-K [D436][D800]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the 26.0% window median from 28.7% in FY2025, in the FY2026 10-K [F50][D766]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether buybacks plus dividends fall below 179.9% of free cash flow in FY2025, in the FY2026 10-K [D445]."}
  ]}
